<Chapter id="common-log" num="08" kicker="A common log" title="Everyone compiles the same material.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      For every domain to reason over the same federation, they need a common place to read the
      material from and a way to check it has not been altered. PolarisChain adopts the
      architecture of <strong>Certificate Transparency</strong>, with another object recorded:
      certificates between CAs, trust lists, and the signed manifests of each version a domain
      activates.
    </p>
    <p>
      Entries are leaves of a Merkle tree, and signed checkpoints allow proofs of inclusion and of
      consistency. The operator can omit an entry but cannot forge one without some proof failing;
      witnesses and monitors make a split view detectable.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="key">A minute book with numbered pages, where one can only write at the end.</p>

  <Figure num={8} caption="Who publishes, who verifies and who decides. Adapted from Annex III of the thesis. The log is specified; its implementation is ongoing work.">
